  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1215 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nSunday night through Friday:\n\nAdditional rounds of storms will be possible Sunday night into \nthe middle of next week as moisture lingers and a couple more \nshortwaves move through. Shear looks plentiful through at least\nMonday to keep an eye on the severe storm potential. The strength\nof the storms for southern Wisconsin will likely in part depend on\nthe timing, as any overnight/early morning storms would likely be\nweaker than afternoon/evening storms. Additionally, precipitable\nwater values of 1.5-2.0\" the first half of next week could lead to\na heavy rain potential, especially the southern Wisconsin sees \nrepeated rounds of storms. Timing of individual rounds of storms \nremains uncertain, but this does look like a potentially active \nstretch given the door will be open to shortwaves while deeper \nmoisture and instability remain across southern Wisconsin. \nTemperatures will likely remain within a couple degrees of normal \nthrough this period. \n\nDDV",
